# camelCase fragments. 'camel' in 'spelloptions' (see init.lua) splits a word at
# every lower-to-upper boundary, so a CamelCase name only passes when each
# fragment does: NumPy is checked as "Num" + "Py", PyTorch as "Py" + "Torch".
# These five are not words on their own -- they exist so those names pass. Add
# to them if a CamelCase name you type keeps flagging; :echo spellbadword('Foo')
# names the offending fragment.
Num
Py
Postgre
Robo
Conv
